This paslang Runtime Library Exception ("Exception") is an additional
permission under section 7 of the GNU General Public License, version
3 ("GPLv3"). It applies to a given file that bears a notice placed by
the copyright holder of the file stating that the file is governed by
GPLv3 along with this Exception.

paslangc, the paslang compiler, puts part of paslang into every
program it compiles: the runtime it writes into its output (the
scheduler of the routines, the collector, the channels, the maps and
the other words of the language) and the units it links with the
program. The intent of this Exception is to allow the programs
compiled with paslang to be propagated under terms of their authors'
choice, while the Runtime Library itself remains free software under
GPLv3.

0. Definitions.

"paslang" means the paslang compiler, paslangc, together with the
Runtime Library, in any version.

"Runtime Library" means any file, or any code in a file, that bears
the notice described above: the units in the src/lib directory of
paslang, in source form and in the compiled forms paslangc makes of
them, and the runtime code that paslangc writes into its output from
src/compiler/pasemit.paslang.

"Target Code" means output from any compiler for a real or virtual
target processor architecture, in executable form or suitable for
input to an assembler, loader, linker and/or execution phase.

A file is an "Independent Module" if it either requires the Runtime
Library for execution after being compiled, or makes use of an
interface provided by the Runtime Library, but is not otherwise based
on the Runtime Library.

1. Grant of Additional Permission.

You have permission to propagate a work of Target Code formed by
compiling Independent Modules with paslang, and by combining them
with the Runtime Library that paslangc writes into its output or
links with it, even if such propagation would otherwise violate the
terms of GPLv3, provided that you comply, for each Independent
Module, with the terms of that module's license. You may convey such
a work under terms of your choice, consistent with the licensing of
the Independent Modules.

2. Scope of the Exception.

This Exception does not apply to the Runtime Library in source form,
nor to paslangc: whoever conveys them, modified or not, does so under
the terms of GPLv3. If you modify a file of the Runtime Library, you
may extend this Exception to your version of the file, but you are
not obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this
Exception's notice from your version.

3. No Weakening of the GPL.

The availability of this Exception does not imply any general
presumption that third-party software is unaffected by the copyleft
requirements of the license of paslang.
